1
00:00:00,270 --> 00:00:02,692
Today we are taking a look at 10 Stack Router.

2
00:00:03,118 --> 00:00:08,164
So 10 Stack Router is a router that you can use to build React and solid applications.

3
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:13,860
And what makes 10 Stack Router special is that it is 100% type safe.

4
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:23,040
So if we take a look here, it offers pretty much the same features that you will find in any other router like in Next.js or in React router.

5
00:00:23,534 --> 00:00:30,532
So we have nested layouts, layout groups, we have file-based routing, parallel data loading, prefetching, and so on.

6
00:00:30,894 --> 00:00:40,708
However, we also have 100% inferred TypeScript support. Everything that we are going to do that is related to navigation is going to be 100% type safe.

7
00:00:41,280 --> 00:00:43,280
We also have stuff like built-in caching.

8
00:00:43,440 --> 00:00:47,840
We're going to take a look at that. You can also integrate it with things like 10 stack query.

9
00:00:48,160 --> 00:00:52,932
It also offers a lot of convenient features when dealing with search parameters.

10
00:00:53,262 --> 00:00:56,000
So we can do things like validating our search parameters.

11
00:00:56,206 --> 00:01:05,380
We can also make our search parameters type safe, and we can also easily manipulate our search parameters in a very easy way, and we're going to take a look at all of that.

12
00:01:05,742 --> 00:01:14,000
We also have other features like context, for example, where we can pass some context, some state that is going to be shared across multiple routes.

13
00:01:14,190 --> 00:01:20,132
We can use it for authentication, for example, to share authentication data in order to protect certain routes.

14
00:01:20,814 --> 00:01:30,628
We also have other features like loading functions or loader functions that we can use in order to load data into our routes. We can also stream data, we can do a lot of stuff.

15
00:01:31,054 --> 00:01:34,480
So let's not talk a lot and let's get started.

16
00:01:34,702 --> 00:01:38,724
And all of these features are going to manifest as we progress through our video.

17
00:01:39,520 --> 00:01:44,400
What you need to know, however, is that 10 stack router is not a framework.

18
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:47,520
So it is not meant to be used as a full stack framework.

19
00:01:47,726 --> 00:01:51,716
However, it is designed to be upgradable to a full stack framework.

20
00:01:52,014 --> 00:01:59,012
And in fact, it is powering 10 stacks full stack framework, which is 10 stack start, which is currently in beta.

21
00:01:59,360 --> 00:02:01,892
This uses React router for routing.

22
00:02:02,080 --> 00:02:11,044
And if you are interested in learning 10 stack start at some point, you will have to be familiar with 10 stack router. So maybe this video is going to be helpful for you.

