01:16:50,592 --> 01:16:54,752
Search parameters are a great way to store the state of your application.

927
01:16:55,182 --> 01:17:01,284
So let's say you have an application that maybe has a lot of filtering, pagination, sorting, and so on.

928
01:17:01,550 --> 01:17:09,312
If you store this information, the information regarding the current page, for example, the current filters and so on in the URL,

929
01:17:09,472 --> 01:17:18,752
this means that you can easily maybe share this URL or bookmark it or open it in a new tab without losing the state since the state lives in the URL.

930
01:17:19,054 --> 01:17:27,792
Unlike when you, for example, store your state or store these information in a React state, once you navigate away from the page or refresh or anything like that,

931
01:17:27,952 --> 01:17:30,116
you are going to lose this state.

932
01:17:30,766 --> 01:17:41,380
So if you have an application that maybe relies heavily on search parameters to do things like filtering, pagination, sorting, and so on, it is important to be able to manage search parameters easily.

933
01:17:41,838 --> 01:17:49,792
Being able to validate search parameters, have type safety for search parameters when you manipulate them, and also be able to store complex data

934
01:17:50,112 --> 01:17:55,812
