01:34:38,478 --> 01:34:46,884
However, you can customize this by passing a couple of functions, parse search and stringify search, and doing custom stuff here.

1122
01:34:47,630 --> 01:34:54,308
So you have some examples here, maybe using base64, you can pass custom functions here.

1123
01:34:54,830 --> 01:34:58,032
You have other examples as well using query string library.

1124
01:34:58,542 --> 01:35:01,764
You can also use it with stringify search and parse search.

1125
01:35:02,510 --> 01:35:07,556
However, in most cases, I guess the default behavior is maybe going to be enough.

1126
01:35:07,918 --> 01:35:13,700
But just know that this exists in case you are in a situation where you need to customize this behavior.

